_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$ is just the length of the interval $[1,2].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=2-1 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}\\,+\\,{x}_{0})({x}_{1}\\,-\\,{x}_{0})\\,+\\,({x}_{2}\\,+\\,{x}_{1})({x}_{2}\\,-\\,{x}_{1})\\,+\\,⋯\\,+\\,({x}_{m}\\,+\\,{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}\\,-\\,{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=2\\cdot 4\\cdot 1=8.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186180275 :question/problem "Let $R = [0, 4] \\cdot [1, 5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = x^{2} + 2y^{2}$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$U ( f , P ) = \\sum _{i = 1}^{m} \\sum _{j = 1}^{n} \\boxed{\\phantom{A A A A A}} \\hspace{0.222em} \\mathrm{\\Delta } {x}_{i} \\mathrm{\\Delta } {y}_{j}$\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" "Let $R = [0, 4] \\cdot [1, 5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y) = x^{2} + 2y^{2}$.\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R$, where\n\n$P_{1} = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}, P_{2} = {y_{0}, y_{1}, …, y_{n}}, P = P_{1} \\cdot P_{2}$.\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n$$\n\\displaystyle U ( f , P ) = \\sum _{i = 1}^{m} \\sum _{j = 1}^{n} \\boxed{\\phantom{A A A A A}} \\hspace{0.222em} \\mathrm{\\Delta } {x}_{i} \\mathrm{\\Delta } {y}_{j}\n$$\nwhere $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$ and $Δy_{j} = y_{j} - y_{j - 1}$, what is the missing expression in the double summation above?"] [:db/cas 17592186180278 :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_(C)\\sin \\left(\\frac{πy}{4}\\right)ds$ along the line segment from $(1, 0, 1)$ to $(2, 2, 3)$." "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_(C)\\sin \\left(\\frac{πy}{4}\\right)ds\n$$ along the line segment from $(1, 0, 1)$ to $(2, 2, 3)$."] [:db/cas 17592186180279 :question/problem "![](images/10/103c586778cdd8181fdc8396a92472df0525fc8e1c77fde9a7c3f731dca6df07.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $OABO,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the counterclockwise direction?" "![](images/10/103c586778cdd8181fdc8396a92472df0525fc8e1c77fde9a7c3f731dca6df07.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $OABO,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the counterclockwise direction?"] [:db/cas 17592186180280 :question/problem "![](images/9f/9fd222d255fd1a37f00cbe7c9abf6af0d0e3af92f9ac581591bb1062780e69fa.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $ABCA,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the **clockwise** direction?" "![](images/9f/9fd222d255fd1a37f00cbe7c9abf6af0d0e3af92f9ac581591bb1062780e69fa.png)\n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the integral $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$ where $C$ is the closed polygonal path $ABCA,$ shown in the diagram above, traversed in the *