))^{2} = 1584$\n\nwhere each $x_{i}$ is a sample observation. Compute an unbiased estimate of the population standard deviation. Round your answer to two decimal places where appropriate.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." "A random sample of size $n = 100$ is conducted from a population. It is known that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle ∑_(i = 1)^(100)(x_{i} - x^(―))^{2} = 1584\n$$\n\nwhere each $x_{i}$ is a sample observation. Compute an unbiased estimate of the population standard deviation. Round your answer to two decimal places where appropriate.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."] [:db/cas 17592186184519 :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1/2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x))=$" "$$\n\\displaystyle {lim}_{x\\to \\,-1/2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x))=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186184526 :question/problem "The complex $4$th roots of the number $z = \\cos \\left(\\frac{π}{3}\\right) + \\textrm{i}\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{3}\\right)$ are given by\n\n$z_{k}^{1/4} = \\cos (\\frac{π}{a} + b \\cdot k) + \\textrm{i}\\sin (\\frac{π}{a} + b \\cdot k)$,\n\nwhere $k = 0, 1, 2, 3$. What are the values of $a$ and $b$?" "The complex $4$th roots of the number $$\n\\displaystyle z = \\cos \\left(\\frac{π}{3}\\right) + \\textrm{i}\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{3}\\right)\n$$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle z_{k}^{1/4} = \\cos (\\frac{π}{a} + b \\cdot k) + \\textrm{i}\\sin (\\frac{π}{a} + b \\cdot k),\n$$\n\nwhere $k = 0, 1, 2, 3$. What are the values of $a$ and $b$?"] [:db/cas 17592186184528 :question/problem "The cube roots of the number $z = \\cos \\left(\\frac{π}{4}\\right) + \\textrm{i}\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{4}\\right)$ are as follows:\n$z_{0}^{1/3} = \\cos ϕ_{0} + \\textrm{i}\\sin ϕ_{0}; z_{1}^{1/3} = \\cos ϕ_{1} + \\textrm{i}\\sin ϕ_{1}; z_{2}^{1/3} = \\cos ϕ_{2} + \\textrm{i}\\sin ϕ_{2}$\nWhat could be the values of $ϕ_{0}$, $ϕ_{1}$, and $ϕ_{2}$?" "The cube roots of the number $$\n\\displaystyle z = \\cos \\left(\\frac{π}{4}\\right) + \\textrm{i}\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{4}\\right)\n$$ are as follows:\n$z_{0}^{1/3} = \\cos ϕ_{0} + \\textrm{i}\\sin ϕ_{0}; z_{1}^{1/3} = \\cos ϕ_{1} + \\textrm{i}\\sin ϕ_{1}; z_{2}^{1/3} = \\cos ϕ_{2} + \\textrm{i}\\sin ϕ_{2}$\nWhat could be the values of $ϕ_{0}$, $ϕ_{1}$, and $ϕ_{2}$?"] [:db/cas 17592186184529 :question/problem "The cube roots of the number $z = 27[\\cos \\left(\\frac{π}{3}\\right) + \\textrm{i}\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{3}\\right)]$ are as follows:\n$z_{0}^{1/3} = r(\\cos ϕ_{0} + \\textrm{i}\\sin ϕ_{0}); z_{1}^{1/3} = r(\\cos ϕ_{1} + \\textrm{i}\\sin ϕ_{1}); z_{2}^{1/3} = r(\\cos ϕ_{2} + \\textrm{i}\\sin ϕ_{2})$\nWhat could be the values of $ϕ_{0}$, $ϕ_{1}$, $ϕ_{2}$ and $r$?" "The cube roots of the number $$\n\\displaystyle z = 27[\\cos \\left(\\frac{π}{3}\\right) + \\textrm{i}\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{3}\\right)]\n$$ are as follows:\n$z_{0}^{1/3} = r(\\cos ϕ_{0} + \\textrm{i}\\sin ϕ_{0}); z_{1}^{1/3} = r(\\cos ϕ_{1} + \\textrm{i}\\sin ϕ_{1}); z_{2}^{1/3} = r(\\cos ϕ_{2} + \\textrm{i}\\sin ϕ_{2})$\nWhat could be the values of $ϕ_{0}$, $ϕ_{1}$, $ϕ_{2}$ and $r$?"] [:db/cas 17592186184530 :question/problem "The complex $5$th roots of the number $z = 32[\\cos \\left(\\frac{π}{6}\\right) + \\textrm{i}\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{6}\\right)]$ are given by\n\n$z_{k}^{1/5} = a[\\cos (\\frac{π}{b} + c \\cdot k) + \\textrm{i}\\sin (\\frac{π}{b} + c \\cdot k)]$,\n\nwhere $k = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4$. What are the values of $a$, $b$, and $b$?" "The complex $5$th roots of the number $$\n\\displaystyle z = 32[\\cos \\left(\\frac{π}{6}\\right) + \\textrm{i}\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{6}\\right)]\n$$ are given by\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle z_{k}^{1/5} = a[\\cos (\\frac{π}{b} + c \\cdot k) + \\textrm{i}\\sin (\\frac{π}{b} + c \\cdot k)],\n$$\n\nwhere $k = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4$. What are the values of $a$, $b$, and $b$?"] [:db/cas 17592186184534 :question/problem "What is $\\sin^{4} \\left(\\frac{π}{2}\\right) - \\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{6}\\right)$